{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Cohere adapter covers the two retrieval steps of a RAG pipeline:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Embeddings"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cohereEmbedding"},{"type":"text","value":"): turn text, images, and fused text+image inputs into vectors with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"embed()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reranking"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cohereRerank"},{"type":"text","value":"): reorder candidate documents by relevance to a query with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rerank()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It does not support "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"summarize()"},{"type":"text","value":", or media generation. Use OpenAI, Anthropic, or Gemini for those. The adapter talks to Cohere's HTTP API directly over "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetch"},{"type":"text","value":", with no SDK dependency."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-cohere\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-cohere\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-cohere\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-cohere\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-cohere\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-cohere\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-cohere\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-cohere\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"embeddings","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Embeddings"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { embed } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { cohereEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-cohere\";\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter: cohereEmbedding(\"embed-v4.0\"),\n  input: [\"a red guitar\", \"a blue drum kit\"],\n  modelOptions: { inputType: \"search_document\" },\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.embeddings[0]?.vector);\nconsole.log(result.usage?.promptTokens);","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inputType"},{"type":"text","value":" is required by Cohere's API. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"search_document"},{"type":"text","value":" at index time and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"search_query"},{"type":"text","value":" at query time (or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"classification"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clustering"},{"type":"text","value":" for those workloads). TanStack AI enforces this at the type level, so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" is required for Cohere embedding calls."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"multimodal-embeddings","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Multimodal Embeddings"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"embed-v4.0 embeds images alongside text. An image part produces an image vector. A nested array of parts ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[textPart, imagePart]"},{"type":"text","value":") fuses text and image into one vector, which suits product catalogs and screenshot search. The outer array is the item list, so nest to fuse:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { embed } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { cohereEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-cohere\";\n\nconst productPhoto = \"iVBORw0KGgo...\"; // base64 image data\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter: cohereEmbedding(\"embed-v4.0\"),\n  input: [\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: {\n        type: \"data\",\n        value: productPhoto,\n        mimeType: \"image/png\",\n      },\n    },\n    // A nested array fuses its parts into a single vector.\n    [\n      { type: \"text\", content: \"Fender Stratocaster, sunburst finish\" },\n      {\n        type: \"image\",\n        source: {\n          type: \"data\",\n          value: productPhoto,\n          mimeType: \"image/png\",\n        },\n      },\n    ],\n  ],\n  modelOptions: { inputType: \"search_document\" },\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.embeddings.length); // 2","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cohere's API does not fetch remote image URLs. Pass base64 data (or a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data:"},{"type":"text","value":" URI), or opt into adapter-side downloading:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { embed } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { cohereEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-cohere\";\n\nconst adapter = cohereEmbedding(\"embed-v4.0\", { allowUrlFetch: true });\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter,\n  input: {\n    type: \"image\",\n    source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/guitar.png\" },\n  },\n  modelOptions: { inputType: \"search_document\" },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"requesting-dimensions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Requesting Dimensions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"embed-v4.0 supports Matryoshka output dimensions via the top-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dimensions"},{"type":"text","value":" option:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { embed } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { cohereEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-cohere\";\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter: cohereEmbedding(\"embed-v4.0\"),\n  input: \"a red guitar\",\n  dimensions: 1024, // 256 | 512 | 1024 | 1536\n  modelOptions: { inputType: \"search_document\" },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"reranking","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reranking"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { rerank } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { cohereRerank } from \"@tanstack/ai-cohere\";\n\nconst { rerankedDocuments } = await rerank({\n  adapter: cohereRerank(\"rerank-v3.5\"),\n  query: \"talk about rain\",\n  documents: [\"sunny day at the beach\", \"rainy afternoon in the city\"],\n});\n\nconsole.log(rerankedDocuments[0]); // 'rainy afternoon in the city'","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For the full reranking guide, with object documents, RAG pipelines, options, and the result shape, see "},{"type":"link","href":"../rerank/rerank","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reranking"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Per-request rerank options go on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { rerank } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { cohereRerank } from \"@tanstack/ai-cohere\";\n\nconst { ranking } = await rerank({\n  adapter: cohereRerank(\"rerank-v3.5\"),\n  query: \"refund policy\",\n  documents: [\"Returns accepted within 30 days.\", \"Free shipping over $50.\"],\n  modelOptions: {\n    maxTokensPerDoc: 512, // Cap tokens kept per document (Cohere default: 4096)\n  },\n});\n\nconsole.log(ranking);","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"models","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Models"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Capability"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"embed-v4.0"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Embeddings"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Multimodal (text + images), Matryoshka "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dimensions"},{"type":"text","value":" support"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rerank-v3.5"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reranking"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Latest multilingual reranker (recommended)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rerank-english-v3.0"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reranking"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"English-optimized reranker"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rerank-multilingual-v3.0"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reranking"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Multilingual reranker"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"environment-variables","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment Variables"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both adapters read your API key from the environment:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"COHERE_API_KEY=your-cohere-api-key","lang":"bash"},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Variable"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"COHERE_API_KEY"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Yes"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your Cohere API key"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Get a key from the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://dashboard.cohere.com/api-keys","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cohere dashboard"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"explicit-api-keys","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Explicit API Keys"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To pass a key directly instead of reading the environment, use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"create*"},{"type":"text","value":" factories:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  createCohereEmbedding,\n  createCohereRerank,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-cohere\";\n\nconst embedAdapter = createCohereEmbedding(\n  \"embed-v4.0\",\n  process.env.MY_COHERE_KEY!,\n);\nconst rerankAdapter = createCohereRerank(\"rerank-v3.5\", \"your-cohere-api-key\");","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"behind-a-proxy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behind a proxy"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Route every request through a gateway, such as Cloudflare AI Gateway or a corporate proxy, with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"baseURL"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultHeaders"},{"type":"text","value":". These two option names are the same on every TanStack AI adapter, so one gateway config works for all of them."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createCohereEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-cohere\";\n\nconst adapter = createCohereEmbedding(\"embed-v4.0\", process.env.COHERE_API_KEY!, {\n  baseURL: \"https://gateway.example.com/cohere\",\n  defaultHeaders: { \"cf-aig-authorization\": `Bearer ${process.env.GATEWAY_TOKEN}` },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"baseUrl"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"headers"},{"type":"text","value":" are aliases of the same two options. If you set both forms, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"baseURL"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultHeaders"},{"type":"text","value":" win."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"api-reference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API Reference"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"cohereembedding-model-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cohereEmbedding(model, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an embedding adapter using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"COHERE_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" from the environment."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"model"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"embed-v4.0\""}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"config.baseURL"},{"type":"text","value":": override the API base URL (default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"https://api.cohere.com"},{"type":"text","value":"). "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"baseUrl"},{"type":"text","value":" is an alias."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"config.defaultHeaders"},{"type":"text","value":": extra request headers. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"headers"},{"type":"text","value":" is an alias."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"config.allowUrlFetch"},{"type":"text","value":": download "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"http(s)"},{"type":"text","value":" image URLs and inline them as base64 (default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createcohereembedding-model-apikey-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createCohereEmbedding(model, apiKey, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Same as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cohereEmbedding"},{"type":"text","value":" with an explicit API key."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"coherererank-model-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cohereRerank(model, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a rerank adapter using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"COHERE_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" from the environment."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"model"},{"type":"text","value":": one of the rerank models above"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"config.baseURL"},{"type":"text","value":": override the API base URL (default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"https://api.cohere.com"},{"type":"text","value":"). "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"baseUrl"},{"type":"text","value":" is an alias."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"config.defaultHeaders"},{"type":"text","value":": extra request headers. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"headers"},{"type":"text","value":" is an alias."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createcoherererank-model-apikey-config","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createCohereRerank(model, apiKey, config?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Same as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cohereRerank"},{"type":"text","value":" with an explicit API key."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next Steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../embeddings.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Embeddings guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":": the full "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"embed()"},{"type":"text","value":" API"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../rerank/rerank","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reranking guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":": full walkthrough including RAG pipelines"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../media/generation-hooks.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generation Hooks"}]},{"type":"text","value":": usage and lifecycle middleware"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"embeddings","text":"Embeddings","level":2},{"id":"multimodal-embeddings","text":"Multimodal Embeddings","level":3},{"id":"requesting-dimensions","text":"Requesting Dimensions","level":3},{"id":"reranking","text":"Reranking","level":2},{"id":"models","text":"Models","level":2},{"id":"environment-variables","text":"Environment Variables","level":2},{"id":"explicit-api-keys","text":"Explicit API Keys","level":2},{"id":"behind-a-proxy","text":"Behind a proxy","level":2},{"id":"api-reference","text":"API Reference","level":2},{"id":"cohereembedding-model-config","text":"cohereEmbedding(model, config?)","level":3},{"id":"createcohereembedding-model-apikey-config","text":"createCohereEmbedding(model, apiKey, config?)","level":3},{"id":"coherererank-model-config","text":"cohereRerank(model, config?)","level":3},{"id":"createcoherererank-model-apikey-config","text":"createCohereRerank(model, apiKey, config?)","level":3},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next Steps","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe Cohere adapter covers the two retrieval steps of a RAG pipeline:\n\n- **Embeddings** (`cohereEmbedding`): turn text, images, and fused text+image inputs into vectors with `embed()`.\n- **Reranking** (`cohereRerank`): reorder candidate documents by relevance to a query with `rerank()`.\n\nIt does not support `chat()`, `summarize()`, or media generation. Use OpenAI, Anthropic, or Gemini for those. The adapter talks to Cohere's HTTP API directly over `fetch`, with no SDK dependency.\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-cohere\nvue: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-cohere\nsolid: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-cohere\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-cohere\npreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-cohere\nangular: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-cohere\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-cohere\noctane: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-cohere\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Embeddings\n\n```typescript\nimport { embed } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { cohereEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-cohere\";\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter: cohereEmbedding(\"embed-v4.0\"),\n  input: [\"a red guitar\", \"a blue drum kit\"],\n  modelOptions: { inputType: \"search_document\" },\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.embeddings[0]?.vector);\nconsole.log(result.usage?.promptTokens);\n```\n\n`inputType` is required by Cohere's API. Use `search_document` at index time and `search_query` at query time (or `classification` / `clustering` for those workloads). TanStack AI enforces this at the type level, so `modelOptions` is required for Cohere embedding calls.\n\n### Multimodal Embeddings\n\nembed-v4.0 embeds images alongside text. An image part produces an image vector. A nested array of parts (`[textPart, imagePart]`) fuses text and image into one vector, which suits product catalogs and screenshot search. The outer array is the item list, so nest to fuse:\n\n```typescript\nimport { embed } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { cohereEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-cohere\";\n\nconst productPhoto = \"iVBORw0KGgo...\"; // base64 image data\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter: cohereEmbedding(\"embed-v4.0\"),\n  input: [\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: {\n        type: \"data\",\n        value: productPhoto,\n        mimeType: \"image/png\",\n      },\n    },\n    // A nested array fuses its parts into a single vector.\n    [\n      { type: \"text\", content: \"Fender Stratocaster, sunburst finish\" },\n      {\n        type: \"image\",\n        source: {\n          type: \"data\",\n          value: productPhoto,\n          mimeType: \"image/png\",\n        },\n      },\n    ],\n  ],\n  modelOptions: { inputType: \"search_document\" },\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.embeddings.length); // 2\n```\n\nCohere's API does not fetch remote image URLs. Pass base64 data (or a `data:` URI), or opt into adapter-side downloading:\n\n```typescript\nimport { embed } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { cohereEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-cohere\";\n\nconst adapter = cohereEmbedding(\"embed-v4.0\", { allowUrlFetch: true });\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter,\n  input: {\n    type: \"image\",\n    source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/guitar.png\" },\n  },\n  modelOptions: { inputType: \"search_document\" },\n});\n```\n\n### Requesting Dimensions\n\nembed-v4.0 supports Matryoshka output dimensions via the top-level `dimensions` option:\n\n```typescript\nimport { embed } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { cohereEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-cohere\";\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter: cohereEmbedding(\"embed-v4.0\"),\n  input: \"a red guitar\",\n  dimensions: 1024, // 256 | 512 | 1024 | 1536\n  modelOptions: { inputType: \"search_document\" },\n});\n```\n\n## Reranking\n\n```typescript\nimport { rerank } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { cohereRerank } from \"@tanstack/ai-cohere\";\n\nconst { rerankedDocuments } = await rerank({\n  adapter: cohereRerank(\"rerank-v3.5\"),\n  query: \"talk about rain\",\n  documents: [\"sunny day at the beach\", \"rainy afternoon in the city\"],\n});\n\nconsole.log(rerankedDocuments[0]); // 'rainy afternoon in the city'\n```\n\nFor the full reranking guide, with object documents, RAG pipelines, options, and the result shape, see [Reranking](../rerank/rerank).\n\nPer-request rerank options go on `modelOptions`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { rerank } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { cohereRerank } from \"@tanstack/ai-cohere\";\n\nconst { ranking } = await rerank({\n  adapter: cohereRerank(\"rerank-v3.5\"),\n  query: \"refund policy\",\n  documents: [\"Returns accepted within 30 days.\", \"Free shipping over $50.\"],\n  modelOptions: {\n    maxTokensPerDoc: 512, // Cap tokens kept per document (Cohere default: 4096)\n  },\n});\n\nconsole.log(ranking);\n```\n\n## Models\n\n| Model                      | Capability | Description                                                       |\n| -------------------------- | ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `embed-v4.0`               | Embeddings | Multimodal (text + images), Matryoshka `dimensions` support        |\n| `rerank-v3.5`              | Reranking  | Latest multilingual reranker (recommended)                         |\n| `rerank-english-v3.0`      | Reranking  | English-optimized reranker                                         |\n| `rerank-multilingual-v3.0` | Reranking  | Multilingual reranker                                              |\n\n## Environment Variables\n\nBoth adapters read your API key from the environment:\n\n```bash\nCOHERE_API_KEY=your-cohere-api-key\n```\n\n| Variable         | Required | Description         |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ------------------- |\n| `COHERE_API_KEY` | Yes      | Your Cohere API key |\n\nGet a key from the [Cohere dashboard](https://dashboard.cohere.com/api-keys).\n\n## Explicit API Keys\n\nTo pass a key directly instead of reading the environment, use the `create*` factories:\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  createCohereEmbedding,\n  createCohereRerank,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-cohere\";\n\nconst embedAdapter = createCohereEmbedding(\n  \"embed-v4.0\",\n  process.env.MY_COHERE_KEY!,\n);\nconst rerankAdapter = createCohereRerank(\"rerank-v3.5\", \"your-cohere-api-key\");\n```\n\n## Behind a proxy\n\nRoute every request through a gateway, such as Cloudflare AI Gateway or a corporate proxy, with `baseURL` and `defaultHeaders`. These two option names are the same on every TanStack AI adapter, so one gateway config works for all of them.\n\n```typescript\nimport { createCohereEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-cohere\";\n\nconst adapter = createCohereEmbedding(\"embed-v4.0\", process.env.COHERE_API_KEY!, {\n  baseURL: \"https://gateway.example.com/cohere\",\n  defaultHeaders: { \"cf-aig-authorization\": `Bearer ${process.env.GATEWAY_TOKEN}` },\n});\n```\n\n`baseUrl` and `headers` are aliases of the same two options. If you set both forms, `baseURL` and `defaultHeaders` win.\n\n## API Reference\n\n### `cohereEmbedding(model, config?)`\n\nCreates an embedding adapter using `COHERE_API_KEY` from the environment.\n\n- `model`: `\"embed-v4.0\"`\n- `config.baseURL`: override the API base URL (default `https://api.cohere.com`). `baseUrl` is an alias.\n- `config.defaultHeaders`: extra request headers. `headers` is an alias.\n- `config.allowUrlFetch`: download `http(s)` image URLs and inline them as base64 (default `false`)\n\n### `createCohereEmbedding(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nSame as `cohereEmbedding` with an explicit API key.\n\n### `cohereRerank(model, config?)`\n\nCreates a rerank adapter using `COHERE_API_KEY` from the environment.\n\n- `model`: one of the rerank models above\n- `config.baseURL`: override the API base URL (default `https://api.cohere.com`). `baseUrl` is an alias.\n- `config.defaultHeaders`: extra request headers. `headers` is an alias.\n\n### `createCohereRerank(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nSame as `cohereRerank` with an explicit API key.\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Embeddings guide](../embeddings.md): the full `embed()` API\n- [Reranking guide](../rerank/rerank): full walkthrough including RAG pipelines\n- [Generation Hooks](../media/generation-hooks.md): usage and lifecycle middleware\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Cohere\nid: cohere-adapter\norder: 11\ndescription: \"Use Cohere with TanStack AI via @tanstack/ai-cohere: embed-v4.0 multimodal embeddings for semantic search and RAG, plus rerank models for relevance.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - cohere\n  - embed-v4\n  - embeddings\n  - multimodal embeddings\n  - semantic search\n  - rerank\n  - reranking\n  - retrieval\n  - adapter\n---\n\nThe Cohere adapter covers the two retrieval steps of a RAG pipeline:\n\n- **Embeddings** (`cohereEmbedding`): turn text, images, and fused text+image inputs into vectors with `embed()`.\n- **Reranking** (`cohereRerank`): reorder candidate documents by relevance to a query with `rerank()`.\n\nIt does not support `chat()`, `summarize()`, or media generation. Use OpenAI, Anthropic, or Gemini for those. The adapter talks to Cohere's HTTP API directly over `fetch`, with no SDK dependency.\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-cohere\nvue: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-cohere\nsolid: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-cohere\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-cohere\npreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-cohere\nangular: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-cohere\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-cohere\noctane: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-cohere\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Embeddings\n\n```typescript\nimport { embed } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { cohereEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-cohere\";\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter: cohereEmbedding(\"embed-v4.0\"),\n  input: [\"a red guitar\", \"a blue drum kit\"],\n  modelOptions: { inputType: \"search_document\" },\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.embeddings[0]?.vector);\nconsole.log(result.usage?.promptTokens);\n```\n\n`inputType` is required by Cohere's API. Use `search_document` at index time and `search_query` at query time (or `classification` / `clustering` for those workloads). TanStack AI enforces this at the type level, so `modelOptions` is required for Cohere embedding calls.\n\n### Multimodal Embeddings\n\nembed-v4.0 embeds images alongside text. An image part produces an image vector. A nested array of parts (`[textPart, imagePart]`) fuses text and image into one vector, which suits product catalogs and screenshot search. The outer array is the item list, so nest to fuse:\n\n```typescript\nimport { embed } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { cohereEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-cohere\";\n\nconst productPhoto = \"iVBORw0KGgo...\"; // base64 image data\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter: cohereEmbedding(\"embed-v4.0\"),\n  input: [\n    {\n      type: \"image\",\n      source: {\n        type: \"data\",\n        value: productPhoto,\n        mimeType: \"image/png\",\n      },\n    },\n    // A nested array fuses its parts into a single vector.\n    [\n      { type: \"text\", content: \"Fender Stratocaster, sunburst finish\" },\n      {\n        type: \"image\",\n        source: {\n          type: \"data\",\n          value: productPhoto,\n          mimeType: \"image/png\",\n        },\n      },\n    ],\n  ],\n  modelOptions: { inputType: \"search_document\" },\n});\n\nconsole.log(result.embeddings.length); // 2\n```\n\nCohere's API does not fetch remote image URLs. Pass base64 data (or a `data:` URI), or opt into adapter-side downloading:\n\n```typescript\nimport { embed } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { cohereEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-cohere\";\n\nconst adapter = cohereEmbedding(\"embed-v4.0\", { allowUrlFetch: true });\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter,\n  input: {\n    type: \"image\",\n    source: { type: \"url\", value: \"https://example.com/guitar.png\" },\n  },\n  modelOptions: { inputType: \"search_document\" },\n});\n```\n\n### Requesting Dimensions\n\nembed-v4.0 supports Matryoshka output dimensions via the top-level `dimensions` option:\n\n```typescript\nimport { embed } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { cohereEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-cohere\";\n\nconst result = await embed({\n  adapter: cohereEmbedding(\"embed-v4.0\"),\n  input: \"a red guitar\",\n  dimensions: 1024, // 256 | 512 | 1024 | 1536\n  modelOptions: { inputType: \"search_document\" },\n});\n```\n\n## Reranking\n\n```typescript\nimport { rerank } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { cohereRerank } from \"@tanstack/ai-cohere\";\n\nconst { rerankedDocuments } = await rerank({\n  adapter: cohereRerank(\"rerank-v3.5\"),\n  query: \"talk about rain\",\n  documents: [\"sunny day at the beach\", \"rainy afternoon in the city\"],\n});\n\nconsole.log(rerankedDocuments[0]); // 'rainy afternoon in the city'\n```\n\nFor the full reranking guide, with object documents, RAG pipelines, options, and the result shape, see [Reranking](../rerank/rerank).\n\nPer-request rerank options go on `modelOptions`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { rerank } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { cohereRerank } from \"@tanstack/ai-cohere\";\n\nconst { ranking } = await rerank({\n  adapter: cohereRerank(\"rerank-v3.5\"),\n  query: \"refund policy\",\n  documents: [\"Returns accepted within 30 days.\", \"Free shipping over $50.\"],\n  modelOptions: {\n    maxTokensPerDoc: 512, // Cap tokens kept per document (Cohere default: 4096)\n  },\n});\n\nconsole.log(ranking);\n```\n\n## Models\n\n| Model                      | Capability | Description                                                       |\n| -------------------------- | ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `embed-v4.0`               | Embeddings | Multimodal (text + images), Matryoshka `dimensions` support        |\n| `rerank-v3.5`              | Reranking  | Latest multilingual reranker (recommended)                         |\n| `rerank-english-v3.0`      | Reranking  | English-optimized reranker                                         |\n| `rerank-multilingual-v3.0` | Reranking  | Multilingual reranker                                              |\n\n## Environment Variables\n\nBoth adapters read your API key from the environment:\n\n```bash\nCOHERE_API_KEY=your-cohere-api-key\n```\n\n| Variable         | Required | Description         |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ------------------- |\n| `COHERE_API_KEY` | Yes      | Your Cohere API key |\n\nGet a key from the [Cohere dashboard](https://dashboard.cohere.com/api-keys).\n\n## Explicit API Keys\n\nTo pass a key directly instead of reading the environment, use the `create*` factories:\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  createCohereEmbedding,\n  createCohereRerank,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-cohere\";\n\nconst embedAdapter = createCohereEmbedding(\n  \"embed-v4.0\",\n  process.env.MY_COHERE_KEY!,\n);\nconst rerankAdapter = createCohereRerank(\"rerank-v3.5\", \"your-cohere-api-key\");\n```\n\n## Behind a proxy\n\nRoute every request through a gateway, such as Cloudflare AI Gateway or a corporate proxy, with `baseURL` and `defaultHeaders`. These two option names are the same on every TanStack AI adapter, so one gateway config works for all of them.\n\n```typescript\nimport { createCohereEmbedding } from \"@tanstack/ai-cohere\";\n\nconst adapter = createCohereEmbedding(\"embed-v4.0\", process.env.COHERE_API_KEY!, {\n  baseURL: \"https://gateway.example.com/cohere\",\n  defaultHeaders: { \"cf-aig-authorization\": `Bearer ${process.env.GATEWAY_TOKEN}` },\n});\n```\n\n`baseUrl` and `headers` are aliases of the same two options. If you set both forms, `baseURL` and `defaultHeaders` win.\n\n## API Reference\n\n### `cohereEmbedding(model, config?)`\n\nCreates an embedding adapter using `COHERE_API_KEY` from the environment.\n\n- `model`: `\"embed-v4.0\"`\n- `config.baseURL`: override the API base URL (default `https://api.cohere.com`). `baseUrl` is an alias.\n- `config.defaultHeaders`: extra request headers. `headers` is an alias.\n- `config.allowUrlFetch`: download `http(s)` image URLs and inline them as base64 (default `false`)\n\n### `createCohereEmbedding(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nSame as `cohereEmbedding` with an explicit API key.\n\n### `cohereRerank(model, config?)`\n\nCreates a rerank adapter using `COHERE_API_KEY` from the environment.\n\n- `model`: one of the rerank models above\n- `config.baseURL`: override the API base URL (default `https://api.cohere.com`). `baseUrl` is an alias.\n- `config.defaultHeaders`: extra request headers. `headers` is an alias.\n\n### `createCohereRerank(model, apiKey, config?)`\n\nSame as `cohereRerank` with an explicit API key.\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Embeddings guide](../embeddings.md): the full `embed()` API\n- [Reranking guide](../rerank/rerank): full walkthrough including RAG pipelines\n- [Generation Hooks](../media/generation-hooks.md): usage and lifecycle middleware\n"}
